@event ww_tree_tobias
# en: The Trees Gossip
title [e401ba] = 树在八卦
# en: Two old trees have their crowns together, whispering. You catch your own name, and then Tobias's. The trees know him: he talks to plants, and plants, it turns out, talk back about him. Something about a hat.
text [054db0] = 两棵老树把树冠凑在一起说悄悄话。你听见了自己的名字，然后是托比亚斯的。树认识他：他跟植物说话，而事实证明，植物也会回过头来议论他。好像跟一顶帽子有关。
# en: Two old trees leaning their crowns together in a misty forest, as if whispering, a student listening beneath.
scene [78fe69] = 雾气弥漫的森林里，两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，像在说悄悄话，一个学生在树下偷听。
# en: Leave them to it; turn back
opt.left.label [4b6247] = 由它们去说吧；往回走
# en: You leave the trees to their gossip and go home. Whatever it was about the hat, it can wait.
opt.left.say.1 [a61e78] = 你让树们继续八卦，自己回家了。不管帽子是怎么回事，都可以等等再说。
# en: Listen in
opt.right.label [70ecdd] = 偷听
# en: Tobias, say the trees, is raising a mandrake called Gerald, who wears a knitted hat and screams softly. They approve of Gerald. They're less sure about the hat.
opt.right.say.1 [e58cd8] = 树们说，托比亚斯在养一株叫杰拉尔德的曼德拉草，它戴着一顶针织帽，叫起来很轻。树们很认可杰拉尔德。对那顶帽子就没那么确定了。

@event ww_tree_lyra
# en: The Trees Gossip
title [e401ba] = 树在八卦
# en: Two old trees have their crowns together, whispering. The name that comes up is Lyra's, and the trees sound amused. One of them has a scorch mark low on its trunk, and it's still a little sore about it.
text [58f941] = 两棵老树把树冠凑在一起说悄悄话。提到的名字是莱拉，树们听起来很乐。其中一棵树干下方有一块焦痕，它到现在还有点耿耿于怀。
# en: Two old trees leaning their crowns together in a misty forest, as if whispering, a student listening beneath.
scene [78fe69] = 雾气弥漫的森林里，两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，像在说悄悄话，一个学生在树下偷听。
# en: Leave them to it; turn back
opt.left.label [4b6247] = 由它们去说吧；往回走
# en: You leave the trees to their gossip. Some things about Lyra you'd rather hear from Lyra.
opt.left.say.1 [94c767] = 你让树们继续八卦。有些关于莱拉的事，你宁愿听莱拉自己说。
# en: Listen in
opt.right.label [70ecdd] = 偷听
# en: Lyra Vaneshade, say the trees, can incinerate a target at forty paces and cannot make toast. She tried, out here, alone, at dawn. The scorched tree was the toast.
opt.right.say.1 [922666] = 树们说，莱拉·凡妮希德能在四十步外把靶子烧成灰，却烤不好一片面包。她试过，就在这儿，独自一人，在黎明时分。那棵烧焦的树，就是那片面包。

@event ww_tree_bram
# en: The Trees Gossip
title [e401ba] = 树在八卦
# en: Two old trees have their crowns together, whispering, and the word you catch is "prefect", said with relish. They know Bram: a red sash comes through here on patrol, they say, and talks to itself about money.
text [379ac3] = 两棵老树把树冠凑在一起说悄悄话，你听到的词是“级长”，说得津津有味。它们认识布拉姆：树们说，有一条红肩带会到这儿来巡逻，还自言自语地念叨钱。
# en: Two old trees leaning their crowns together in a misty forest, as if whispering, a student listening beneath.
scene [78fe69] = 雾气弥漫的森林里，两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，像在说悄悄话，一个学生在树下偷听。
# en: Leave them to it; turn back
opt.left.label [4b6247] = 由它们去说吧；往回走
# en: You leave the trees to their gossip. Bram has enough people talking about him.
opt.left.say.1 [d34255] = 你让树们继续八卦。议论布拉姆的人已经够多了。
# en: Listen in
opt.right.label [70ecdd] = 偷听
# en: Bram, say the trees, once invented a hall tax for the east staircase, and collected it for a week before anyone checked. They think it was very enterprising. They would.
opt.right.say.1 [808303] = 树们说，布拉姆曾经给东楼梯发明过一种“过厅税”，收了一个星期才有人去查。它们觉得这很有进取心。它们当然会这么觉得。

@event ww_tree_mir
# en: The Trees Gossip
title [e401ba] = 树在八卦
# en: Two old trees have their crowns together, whispering about a bird that isn't a bird. It ticks, they say. It flew through here once with Mir chasing it and shouting about a deadline.
text [53d7f1] = 两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，悄悄议论一只不是鸟的鸟。它会滴答响，树们说。有一次它从这儿飞过，米尔在后面追着它，嚷嚷着什么截止日期。
# en: Two old trees leaning their crowns together in a misty forest, as if whispering, a student listening beneath.
scene [78fe69] = 雾气弥漫的森林里，两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，像在说悄悄话，一个学生在树下偷听。
# en: Leave them to it; turn back
opt.left.label [4b6247] = 由它们去说吧；往回走
# en: You leave the trees to their gossip, and go home listening for ticking.
opt.left.say.1 [3f72d2] = 你让树们继续八卦，回家的路上一直竖着耳朵听有没有滴答声。
# en: Listen in
opt.right.label [70ecdd] = 偷听
# en: Mir, say the trees, built a clockwork owl that remembers deadlines, birthdays, and grudges, slightly. The owl landed here and told an oak it was overdue. The oak is still upset.
opt.right.say.1 [ab36b8] = 树们说，米尔造了一只发条猫头鹰，它记得截止日期、生日，还有一点点仇。那只猫头鹰在这儿落过脚，告诉一棵橡树它逾期了。那棵橡树到现在还不痛快。

@event ww_tree_kael
# en: The Trees Gossip
title [e401ba] = 树在八卦
# en: Two old trees are whispering, and one side of each trunk is frosted, as if someone leaned there. The Northern boy, they say. He walks out here when he can't sleep, and puts his hands on their bark.
text [a211d8] = 两棵老树在说悄悄话，每棵树干的一侧都结着霜，像有人在那儿靠过。北方来的那个男孩，它们说。他睡不着的时候就走到这儿来，把手放在它们的树皮上。
# en: Two old trees leaning their crowns together in a misty forest, frost on one side of their trunks, a student listening.
scene [6ed471] = 雾气弥漫的森林里，两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，树干一侧结着霜，一个学生在树下偷听。
# en: Leave them to it; turn back
opt.left.label [4b6247] = 由它们去说吧；往回走
# en: You leave the trees to their whispering. It feels like his to tell.
opt.left.say.1 [db0d8d] = 你让树们继续低语。这感觉该由他自己来说。
# en: Listen in
opt.right.label [70ecdd] = 偷听
# en: His hands are always cold, the trees say. He puts them on the bark to see if anything is ever warm enough. Nothing has been, yet. The trees sound sorry about it.
opt.right.say.1 [8434af] = 他的手总是冰的，树们说。他把手放在树皮上，看有没有什么东西能暖得过来。到现在还没有。树们听起来为此感到抱歉。

@event ww_tree_nessa
# en: The Trees Gossip
title [e401ba] = 树在八卦
# en: Two old trees are whispering about a quill. Somebody's quill was left out here overnight, they say, and by morning it had written a headline on a birch. The birch would like a retraction.
text [66da0d] = 两棵老树在悄悄议论一支羽毛笔。有人的羽毛笔在这儿落了一夜，树们说，到了早上，它已经在一棵白桦上写好了一条头条新闻。那棵白桦希望登报更正。
# en: Two old trees leaning their crowns together in a misty forest, a quill-scratched message on one trunk, a student listening.
scene [8876b5] = 雾气弥漫的森林里，两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，其中一棵树干上刻着羽毛笔划出的字，一个学生在偷听。
# en: Leave them to it; turn back
opt.left.label [4b6247] = 由它们去说吧；往回走
# en: You leave the trees to their gossip, which is at least partly about the press.
opt.left.say.1 [639d37] = 你让树们继续八卦，它们至少有一部分在议论新闻界。
# en: Listen in
opt.right.label [70ecdd] = 偷听
# en: Nessa's quill, say the trees, starts inventing the news if she leaves it unsupervised. The birch's headline is about the birch. It's very unflattering, and, the trees admit, mostly true.
opt.right.say.1 [b2c334] = 树们说，内莎的羽毛笔要是没人看着，就会开始编新闻。那棵白桦上的头条写的就是那棵白桦。很不客气，而且，树们承认，大体属实。

@event ww_tree_corvin
# en: The Trees Gossip
title [e401ba] = 树在八卦
# en: Two old trees are whispering, and laughing, in the creaking way trees laugh. It's about Corvin. It's about a debt. It's about, as far as you can make out, a goat.
text [dca147] = 两棵老树在说悄悄话，还在笑，是树那种嘎吱嘎吱的笑法。是关于科尔文的。是关于一笔债的。就你能听明白的部分来说，是关于一只山羊的。
# en: Two old trees leaning their crowns together in a misty forest, a goat grazing beneath, a student listening.
scene [4d87f8] = 雾气弥漫的森林里，两棵老树把树冠凑在一起，树下一只山羊在吃草，一个学生在偷听。
# en: Leave them to it; turn back
opt.left.label [4b6247] = 由它们去说吧；往回走
# en: You leave the trees laughing. You'll hear about the goat eventually. Everyone does.
opt.left.say.1 [0879ea] = 你让树们笑着。你迟早会听说那只山羊的。每个人都会。
# en: Listen in
opt.right.label [70ecdd] = 偷听
# en: Corvin, say the trees, once owed thirty crowns to trolls, and offered to pay them back with a goat. The trolls took the goat. The goat now runs the trolls.
opt.right.say.1 [345a19] = 树们说，科尔文曾经欠了巨魔三十克朗，提出用一只山羊来还。巨魔收下了山羊。现在那只山羊管着巨魔。

@event ww_tree_tell
# en: Something the Trees Said
title [b8e74e] = 树说过的事
# en: {npc} is right there, and you know something about {them} that {they} didn't tell you. The Whisperwood did. It's on the tip of your tongue.
text [db8a12] = {npc}就在那儿，而你知道一件关于{them}的事，是{they}没告诉过你的。是低语森林告诉你的。话就在嘴边。
# en: Two students talking in a castle corridor, one looking surprised and caught out, the other trying not to smile.
scene [758852] = 城堡走廊里两个学生在说话，一个一脸惊讶、像被抓了个现行，另一个努力忍着不笑。
# en: Keep it to yourself
opt.left.label [09de43] = 自己留着
# en: You keep it. Whatever the trees say, it's {npc}'s to tell. It sits in you like a small warm stone.
opt.left.say.1 [4fd816] = 你没说。不管树们怎么讲，那都该由{npc}自己来说。它在你心里，像一块温热的小石头。
# en: Tell {them} you heard it
opt.right.label [cce0c0] = 告诉{them}你听说了
# en: {npc_is(tobias): Tobias goes pink to the ears. "They told you about Gerald?" Then, proudly: "Do you want to meet him?"|{npc_is(mir): "The owl went to the WOOD?" Mir is delighted. "It's famous. It's going to be unbearable."|{npc_is(corvin): Corvin laughs until he has to lean on the wall. "The goat," he says. "Everyone always hears about the goat."|{npc_is(kael): Kael is quiet for a long moment. Then he holds out a hand, and you take it. "Not yet," he says. "But warmer."|{npc_is(lyra): Lyra turns the colour of her own fire. "Trees," she says, "are liars," and stalks off, and doesn't speak to you until Thursday.|{npc_is(bram): Bram goes rigid. "That was a legitimate levy," he says, and writes something down that is probably your name.|Nessa narrows her eyes. "Who's your source? A tree. A TREE." She writes it down anyway.}}}}}}
opt.right.say.1 [95bf60] = {npc_is(tobias): 托比亚斯的耳朵都红了。“它们跟你说了杰拉尔德？”然后，骄傲地：“你想见见他吗？”|{npc_is(mir): “那只猫头鹰去了森林？”米尔高兴坏了。“它出名了。它会变得让人受不了的。”|{npc_is(corvin): 科尔文笑得不得不扶着墙。“那只山羊，”他说。“每个人最后都会听说那只山羊。”|{npc_is(kael): 凯尔沉默了很久。然后他伸出一只手，你握住了。“还没有，”他说。“不过暖和些了。”|{npc_is(lyra): 莱拉的脸红得跟她的火一样。“树，”她说，“都是骗子，”然后大步走开，到星期四之前都没跟你说话。|{npc_is(bram): 布拉姆浑身僵住。“那是合法的征收，”他说，然后写下了什么，多半是你的名字。|内莎眯起眼睛。“你的消息来源是谁？一棵树。一棵树！”她还是把它记下来了。}}}}}}

@event jit_maud_warning
# en: Maud's Warning
title [5e3c78] = 莫德的忠告
# en: Old Maud is at the edge of the wood with a basket, and catches your sleeve. "Off the path, are we? Listen, dearie. Press on as far as you like, turn back whenever you like, and what you bring out, Pell will buy. Fall once and you'll get up. Twice, and someone'll have to come and find you."
text [04432e] = 老莫德挎着篮子站在林子边上，一把拉住你的袖子。“离开小路了，是吧？听着，亲爱的。想往里走多远都行，想什么时候回头都行，带出来的东西，佩尔都会收。摔一跤，你还能爬起来。摔两跤，就得有人去找你了。”
# en: An old woman in a shawl with a basket of mushrooms catching a student's sleeve at the edge of a misty forest.
scene [0bb50e] = 雾气弥漫的森林边缘，一位披着披肩、挎着一篮蘑菇的老妇人拉住一个学生的袖子。
# en: Thank her
opt.left.label [c00500] = 谢谢她
# en: "And mind the Hush," she adds, letting go. "It keeps the castle's hours. It wakes when you're meant to be asleep."
opt.left.say.1 [81d34f] = “还有，当心寂境，”她松开手时又补了一句。“它守的是城堡的时辰。你该睡觉的时候，它就醒了。”
# en: Ask about the deep part
opt.right.label [0e616f] = 问问深处的事
# en: "The Hush," she says. "Past the heartwood. It keeps the castle's hours, dearie: it wakes at midnight, when you're meant to be asleep." She looks at the wood a long moment. "Don't go down there without a friend."
opt.right.say.1 [427783] = “寂境，”她说。“在心木林再往里。它守的是城堡的时辰，亲爱的：午夜才醒，正是你该睡觉的时候。”她望着森林看了很久。“别一个人下去。”

@event brask_deep_hours
# en: Midnight Hours
title [6200fa] = 午夜的时辰
# en: Professor Brask is feeding the old barn owl in the loft. "You've been in the wood," she says, without turning round. "By day, I hope. The deep things keep midnight hours. Most of them would rather you didn't."
text [61eeda] = 布拉斯克教授在阁楼上喂那只老仓鸮。“你去过林子了，”她头也不回地说。“但愿是白天去的。深处的东西守的是午夜的时辰。它们大多不希望你去。”
# en: A professor in a riding coat feeding a barn owl in a dim stable loft at dusk, the forest dark through the window.
scene [cf0119] = 黄昏时分，昏暗的马厩阁楼里，一位穿骑装的教授在喂一只仓鸮，窗外的森林一片漆黑。
# en: Ask her what deep things
opt.left.label [6c281e] = 问她是什么深处的东西
# en: "Old ones," says Brask. "In the Hush, past the heartwood. Wakes at midnight. Go down by day and it's just quiet." She feeds the owl another mouse. "That was a warning, not an invitation." It didn't sound like either.
opt.left.say.1 [d38093] = “老东西，”布拉斯克说。“在寂境里，心木林再往里。午夜才醒。白天下去，那儿只是安静。”她又喂了猫头鹰一只老鼠。“这是警告，不是邀请。”可听起来两样都不像。
# en: Help with the owl instead
opt.right.label [8c3f95] = 还是帮忙喂猫头鹰吧
# en: You hold the bucket and the owl regards you with deep contempt. Brask says nothing more about the wood, and you leave with a peck on the thumb and her good opinion.
opt.right.say.1 [912a71] = 你拎着桶，猫头鹰用深深的鄙夷打量着你。布拉斯克没再提林子的事，你离开时拇指上挨了一啄，也赢得了她的好感。

@event carto_hush_margin
# en: A Note in the Margin
title [e2dcc2] = 页边的笔记
# en: The Cartographers' oldest map of the grounds has a margin crowded with notes in a dozen hands. Over the Whisperwood someone has written, very small: "W. wood: HUSH. Twelfth bell only." Corvin taps it. "Never checked that one," he says. "Nobody's that brave. Or that stupid."
text [e65e76] = 午夜制图社最老的那张校园地图，页边挤满了十几种笔迹的批注。在低语森林上方，有人写得很小：“西林：寂境。只在第十二声钟响。”科尔文敲了敲那行字。“这条从没查证过，”他说。“没人那么勇敢。或者那么蠢。”
# en: An old hand-drawn map of a forest spread on a table by candlelight, one margin crowded with tiny ink notes.
scene [aacac8] = 烛光下，一张手绘的旧森林地图摊在桌上，一侧页边挤满了细小的墨水批注。
# en: Ink it onto the new map
opt.left.label [a4f927] = 把它誊到新地图上
# en: You copy the note onto the new map in your neatest hand, and the Cartographers watch you do it with the particular silence of people placing bets.
opt.left.say.1 [794e00] = 你用最工整的字迹把这条批注誊到新地图上，制图社的人看着你写，那种安静，像一群正在下注的人。
# en: Leave the margin alone
opt.right.label [21309c] = 别动那页边
# en: You leave the old note where it is. The Cartographers move on to the third floor's missing corridor. The margin stays in your head anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [9dfcea] = 你把那条旧批注留在原处。制图社转而去研究三楼那条失踪的走廊。可那行页边的字还是留在了你脑子里。

@event grimsbys_field_guide
# en: A Field Guide
title [515800] = 野外图鉴
# en: Grimsby has put a field guide to the western woods on the counter, open at moonpetal. There's a long footnote, in tiny print, and someone has circled it. "I think," says Grimsby mildly, "that you should read the footnote."
text [e73338] = 格林斯比在柜台上放了一本西部林地的野外图鉴，翻开在月瓣花那一页。那里有一条长长的脚注，字很小，有人把它圈了出来。“我想，”格林斯比温和地说，“你该读读那条脚注。”
# en: A small battered green field guide open on a bookshop counter, a long footnote circled in pencil.
scene [96d2d5] = 书店柜台上摊着一本破旧的绿色小图鉴，一条长脚注被铅笔圈了出来。
# en: Buy the book
opt.left.label [c7f915] = 买下这本书
# en: The footnote says moonpetal in the deep wood opens only "in the Hush, at the twelfth bell". You buy the book and read the rest on the way home. It's mostly about mushrooms, and very good.
opt.left.say.1 [888936] = 脚注说，深林里的月瓣花只在“寂境之中、第十二声钟响时”开放。你买下书，在回家路上读完了剩下的部分。大半是讲蘑菇的，写得非常好。
# en: Read the footnote and go
opt.right.label [840a0b] = 读完脚注就走
# en: You read the footnote standing up: moonpetal in the deep wood opens only "in the Hush, at the twelfth bell". Grimsby closes the book with a sigh that says browsers are a cross he bears.
opt.right.say.1 [c4fbb5] = 你站着读完了脚注：深林里的月瓣花只在“寂境之中、第十二声钟响时”开放。格林斯比合上书，叹了口气，意思是光看不买的人是他背负的十字架。

@event maud_tuppence
# en: My Girl in the Hush
title [1605d7] = 我那住在寂境的姑娘
# en: Over tea, Maud nods at a drawing pinned over the stove: a spider, no bigger than a hand. "My Tuppence," she says. "Found her in the greenhouses, my first winter as groundskeeper. Kept her in the potting shed till she got too big for it. She's in the Hush now, the deep part of the wood. Keeps the worse things out." She sips. "Only wakes at midnight, the Hush."
text [605cc2] = 喝茶的时候，莫德朝炉子上方钉着的一张画点了点头：一只蜘蛛，不比一只手大。“我的塔彭丝，”她说。“在温室里捡到的，我当园丁的头一个冬天。养在育苗棚里，直到她长得装不下。现在她在寂境，林子最深的地方。把更糟的东西挡在外面。”她抿了一口茶。“寂境只在午夜才醒。”
# en: An old woman pouring tea in a cluttered cottage kitchen, an old drawing of a tiny spider pinned above the stove.
scene [6a84e2] = 杂乱的小屋厨房里，一位老妇人在倒茶，炉子上方钉着一张小蜘蛛的旧画。
# en: Ask how big she is now
opt.left.label [a2483c] = 问她现在有多大
# en: "Oh, carriage-sized," says Maud fondly. "Bit more." She pours more tea. You find you don't want any.
opt.left.say.1 [8d58a0] = “噢，马车那么大，”莫德慈爱地说。“还大一点。”她又倒了些茶。你发现自己一口也不想喝了。
# en: Ask if she misses her
opt.right.label [6e0e36] = 问她想不想她
# en: "Every day," says Maud. "But you can't keep a thing in a potting shed because you'd miss it. That's not love, that's a jar." She looks at you over the cup. "Tell her I said hello, if you're ever that foolish."
opt.right.say.1 [8b7f57] = “天天想，”莫德说。“可你不能因为舍不得，就把一样东西关在育苗棚里。那不叫爱，那叫罐子。”她从杯沿上方看着你。“要是你哪天真蠢到那份上，替我跟她问声好。”

@event maud_worse_out
# en: She Kept Worse Out
title [b71f8b] = 她把更糟的挡在外面
# en: Maud knows. Of course she knows: the bees told her, or the wood did. "You beat my Tuppence," she says, and she's proud, you can hear it, and frightened too. "Good for you, dearie. Only she kept worse things out. Now she's let one in. Sits by a lantern, I hear. Polite." She doesn't say his name.
text [90a84e] = 莫德知道了。她当然知道：是蜜蜂告诉她的，或者是林子。“你打赢了我的塔彭丝，”她说，听得出她很骄傲，也很害怕。“好样的，亲爱的。只是她一直把更糟的东西挡在外面。现在她放进来了一个。听说坐在一盏灯笼旁边。很有礼貌。”她没说他的名字。
# en: An old woman standing at her cottage door at dusk, looking toward a dark forest with an expression half proud, half afraid.
scene [4ca456] = 黄昏时分，一位老妇人站在小屋门口，望着漆黑的森林，神情一半骄傲，一半害怕。
# en: Promise to be careful
opt.left.label [73c3d8] = 保证会小心
# en: "Careful," says Maud, "is what people say instead of 'not going'." But she pats your hand, and gives you a jar of honey for the road you haven't said you'll take.
opt.left.say.1 [e8d43d] = “小心，”莫德说，“是人们不想说‘不去’时才说的话。”可她还是拍了拍你的手，给了你一罐蜂蜜，让你带着上那条你还没说要走的路。
# en: Ask who he is
opt.right.label [15bdc3] = 问他是谁
# en: "Somebody they sent away," says Maud, "before my time, almost. He was clever. They always are." She shuts the door very firmly, as if on a draught.
opt.right.say.1 [908be9] = “一个被他们送走的人，”莫德说，“差不多在我来之前。他很聪明。他们总是很聪明。”她把门关得很紧，像在挡穿堂风。

@event ww_mastery_map
# en: Maud's Old Map
title [cc4ecb] = 莫德的旧地图
# en: Maud slides a creased old map across the table. The Whisperwood, drawn in her young hand, every carved bee marked, every path to the heartwood, and a careful line down into the Hush. "Mine," she says, "from when I used to go down to visit. My knees won't take it now. Yours will."
text [661d71] = 莫德把一张皱巴巴的旧地图推过桌面。低语森林，出自她年轻时的手笔，每一只刻着的蜜蜂都标了出来，每一条通往心木林的路，还有一条小心画下的线，一直通到寂境里。“我的，”她说，“以前我常下去看她。现在我的膝盖受不了了。你的还行。”
# en: An old woman handing a creased, hand-drawn map of a forest to a student across a cottage table.
scene [0a0925] = 小屋的桌旁，一位老妇人把一张皱巴巴的手绘森林地图递给一个学生。
# en: Take it, gratefully
opt.left.label [6ab2d2] = 心怀感激地收下
# en: You fold it into your coat. From now on, at midnight, you can go straight down past the heartwood. "Bring it back," says Maud, "when you're old."
opt.left.say.1 [c55e9e] = 你把它折好放进外套里。从今往后，午夜时你可以直接下到心木林以下。“等你老了，”莫德说，“再还给我。”
# en: Ask her to come with you, once
opt.right.label [da9c48] = 请她陪你去一次
# en: She laughs till she coughs. "Once," she says. And one night she does, slowly, on your arm, as far as the heartwood, and stands there smiling at the dark. Then she gives you the map.
opt.right.say.1 [897f31] = 她笑得咳嗽起来。“就一次，”她说。有一天晚上她真的去了，慢慢地，挽着你的胳膊，一直走到心木林，站在那儿对着黑暗微笑。然后她把地图给了你。

@event offer_heartwood_wand
# en: Mir Carves the Heartwood
title [ed25cb] = 米尔雕心木
# en: Mir is at the market stall, mending a clockwork hen, when you put the heartwood splinter on the counter. They stop. They pick it up as if it might bite, then as if it might sing. "Where," they say, "did you get THIS?" Then: "I can carve it. It's work. Not much money."
text [3ad44d] = 米尔正在集市摊子上修一只发条母鸡，你把心木木片放在了柜台上。TA停住了。TA把它拿起来，先像怕它咬人，又像怕它唱歌。“你从哪儿，”TA说，“弄到这个的？”然后：“我能雕。是个活儿。不怎么收钱。”
# en: An artificer at a market stall turning a red-gold splinter of wood in their fingers, a carving knife ready.
scene [eafbbe] = 集市摊子前，一位工匠用手指转动着一片红金色的木片，雕刻刀已经备好。
# en: Not yet
opt.left.label [8dd27c] = 先不用
# en: Mir hands it back with real reluctance. "Don't lose it," they say. "Don't use it to stir anything. Don't..." You leave while they're still listing.
opt.left.say.1 [26a67c] = 米尔极不情愿地把它还给你。“别弄丢了，”TA说。“别拿它搅东西。别……”TA还在列的时候，你就走了。
# en: Have Mir carve it
opt.right.label [3e2515] = 请米尔雕它
# en: A wand for fights: more Mana.
opt.right.hint [74763c] = 一根战斗用的魔杖：更多魔力。
# en: Mir carves it in an evening, talking to it the whole time. The grain moves under their knife as if it's helping. When they hand it over, it's warm, and so are their hands. "Don't tell anyone I made a thing that isn't a machine," they say.
opt.right.say.1 [7a8145] = 米尔花了一个晚上雕它，一边雕一边跟它说话。木纹在刀下游动，好像在帮忙。TA递给你的时候，它是温的，TA的手也是。“别告诉别人我做了个不是机器的东西，”TA说。

@event offer_spinner_silk_robe
# en: Spinner Silk
title [8231f7] = 织网者的丝
# en: The village tailor unrolls the Spinner's silk across her table and goes very quiet. She holds it to the window. Light goes into it and doesn't come out. "I can make you a robe of this," she says at last. "It will cost you. Not for the silk. For my nerves."
text [d43853] = 村里的裁缝把织网者的丝在桌上展开，一下子安静了。她把它举到窗前。光照进去，就没再出来。“我能用这个给你做件长袍，”她终于说。“会很贵。不是贵在丝。是贵在我的神经。”
# en: A village tailor holding up a length of shimmering grey silk to the window light, her mouth open in astonishment.
scene [48cb36] = 一位村里的裁缝把一段闪着微光的灰色丝绸举到窗前的光里，惊讶得合不拢嘴。
# en: Keep the silk for now
opt.left.label [e0ca3f] = 丝先留着
# en: She rolls it up again, very carefully, as if it might roll her up. "Come back," she says. "Please come back. I want to have made it."
opt.left.say.1 [043b06] = 她又把它卷起来，非常小心，好像怕它反过来把她卷起来。“回来，”她说。“请一定回来。我想做过这件东西。”
# en: Have the robe made
opt.right.label [d6d213] = 请她做长袍
# en: A robe for fights: much more Health, quicker steps.
opt.right.hint [d0d7c1] = 一件战斗用的长袍：多得多的生命，步子更快。
# en: It takes her a week and two sleepless nights. When you put it on, you move like a rumour. The tailor sits down. "I'll never make anything like it again," she says, happily.
opt.right.say.1 [1a0874] = 她花了一个星期，熬了两个通宵。你穿上它，走起路来像一则传闻。裁缝坐了下来。“我再也做不出这样的东西了，”她开心地说。

@event item_quill_brask
# en: Brask Knows That Owl
title [247d21] = 布拉斯克认得那只猫头鹰
# en: Professor Brask sees your quill and takes it out of your hand without asking. She turns it to the light. Above you, in the rafters, the old barn owl shifts. "That's hers," says Brask. "From the winter she moulted in the wood. I looked for that feather for a month."
text [8e5496] = 布拉斯克教授看见你的羽毛笔，不由分说就从你手里拿了过去。她把它转向光。在你头顶的椽子上，那只老仓鸮挪了挪身子。“这是她的，”布拉斯克说。“她在林子里换羽的那个冬天掉的。那根羽毛我找了一个月。”
# en: A professor in a riding coat holding up a white owl-feather quill to the light, an old barn owl in the rafters above.
scene [e59717] = 一位穿骑装的教授把一支白色猫头鹰羽毛笔举向光亮，上方椽子上蹲着一只老仓鸮。
# en: Offer it back
opt.left.label [57406d] = 把它还给她
# en: Brask looks at the quill a long time, then hands it back. "Keep it. She'd want it used." Then, gruffly, she tells you how old the owl is, and how many colleagues it has outlived, and doesn't say which loss hurt most.
opt.left.say.1 [476bbf] = 布拉斯克看着那支笔看了很久，然后还给了你。“留着吧。她会希望它被用上。”然后，她粗声粗气地告诉你那只猫头鹰有多老，送走了多少同事，却没说哪一次离别最痛。
# en: Ask her about the owl
opt.right.label [cf6e1d] = 问她那只猫头鹰的事
# en: "Older than the beastcraft syllabus," says Brask. "Outlived three professors." She hands back the quill. "Wouldn't say which one I miss most," she says, and then doesn't.
opt.right.say.1 [3672e3] = “比魔兽学的教学大纲还老，”布拉斯克说。“送走了三位教授。”她把笔还给你。“不会告诉你我最想念哪一个，”她说，然后果然没说。

@event item_quill_nessa
# en: The Quill Writes Back
title [189326] = 羽毛笔回嘴了
# en: You leave your owl quill on Nessa's desk for one minute. When you come back, her enchanted quill and yours are writing at each other on a sheet of foolscap: hers in headlines, yours in very tidy footnotes. It is, as far as you can tell, an argument about accuracy.
text [9200ac] = 你把猫头鹰羽毛笔在内莎桌上放了一分钟。等你回来，她那支施了魔法的羽毛笔正和你的笔在一张大页纸上对着写：她的写标题，你的写非常工整的脚注。就你能看出来的，这是一场关于准确性的争论。
# en: Two quills scratching furiously at each other on a sheet of paper in a cluttered newspaper office, a student and an editor watching aghast.
scene [83cbae] = 杂乱的报社办公室里，两支羽毛笔在一张纸上激烈地互相书写，一个学生和一个编辑目瞪口呆地看着。
# en: Let them finish
opt.left.label [726d27] = 让它们写完
# en: Nessa reads the finished sheet aloud. Her quill invented a scandal; yours corrected it, line by line. "I'm printing this," says Nessa, "as a warning to my quill."
opt.left.say.1 [bfb506] = 内莎把写完的那张纸大声念了出来。她的笔编了一桩丑闻；你的笔逐行把它更正了。“我要把这个登出来，”内莎说，“给我的笔一个警告。”
# en: Separate them
opt.right.label [b77b0a] = 把它们分开
# en: You pull your quill away mid-footnote. Nessa's quill sulks for a week and invents nothing, which Nessa says is worse.
opt.right.say.1 [8c3a4d] = 你在脚注写到一半时把笔拿开了。内莎的笔赌气赌了一个星期，什么都没编，内莎说这更糟。

@event item_lodestone_kael
# en: North, Always North
title [1983ce] = 北方，永远是北方
# en: Kael notices the lodestone turning on its cord, slowly, to face north. He watches it for a long moment. "It points home," he says. "My home." He doesn't sound as if he's decided how he feels about that.
text [12c914] = 凯尔注意到磁石在绳子上慢慢转动，转向北方。他看了它很久。“它指着家，”他说。“我的家。”听起来他还没决定自己对此是什么感觉。
# en: A pale Northern student looking at a dark pendant turning slowly on a cord, his frosted hand held out beneath it.
scene [3eb168] = 一个苍白的北方学生看着一只深色吊坠在绳子上缓缓转动，他结着霜的手托在下面。
# en: Let him hold it
opt.left.label [c4aede] = 让他拿着
# en: He holds it in his cold palm and the stone keeps turning north, steady as a promise. "It doesn't know I left," he says, and gives it back.
opt.left.say.1 [6d883b] = 他把它托在冰冷的掌心里，石头依然转向北方，稳得像一个承诺。“它不知道我已经离开了，”他说，把它还给了你。
# en: Ask about the North
opt.right.label [2b1b3f] = 问问北方的事
# en: "Cold," says Kael, which is the whole answer, and the subject is closed. The pendant keeps pointing at it.
opt.right.say.1 [4de6c2] = “冷，”凯尔说，这就是全部的回答，话题到此为止。吊坠还在指着那个方向。

@event item_lodestone_stacks
# en: Lost in the Stacks
title [8eca0e] = 迷失在书库
# en: In the deep stacks the lodestone stops pointing north and starts pointing at a shelf. Then at a book, misshelved forty years ago between two treatises on drainage. It's very old, and very interesting, and nobody has missed it.
text [2a2dd2] = 在书库深处，磁石不再指向北方，而是开始指向一个书架。然后指向一本书，四十年前被放错了地方，夹在两本排水论著中间。它很老，很有意思，而且没有人想念过它。
# en: A student following a turning pendant between tall dim library shelves, a misshelved book glowing faintly at the end of a row.
scene [15a96d] = 一个学生跟着一只转动的吊坠穿行在高大昏暗的图书馆书架间，一排尽头一本放错位置的书微微发着光。
# en: Read it here and now
opt.left.label [5057ed] = 就在这儿读
# en: You read it on the floor of the stacks until the lamps are put out. It's about the wood. Most of it you already knew, the hard way.
opt.left.say.1 [093dc1] = 你坐在书库地板上读，直到灯被熄掉。书是讲林子的。大部分你已经知道了，是吃过苦头才知道的。
# en: Return it to its shelf
opt.right.label [36b1d3] = 把它放回原位
# en: You find where it belongs and put it there. Grimsby, when you tell him, is so pleased he gives you tea.
opt.right.say.1 [ab4739] = 你找到它该在的地方，把它放了回去。你告诉格林斯比的时候，他高兴得请你喝了茶。

@event item_tine_brask
# en: Brask Bows to It
title [fde4ad] = 布拉斯克向它鞠躬
# en: Professor Brask sees the stag's tine at your belt and stops in the middle of a sentence. Then she bows to it, deeply, the way she bows in the bracken. Every horse in the stable goes quiet.
text [3d87cf] = 布拉斯克教授看见你腰间的鹿角尖，话说到一半停住了。然后她向它深深鞠了一躬，就像她在蕨丛里鞠躬那样。马厩里的每一匹马都安静了下来。
# en: A sturdy professor bowing low to a dark antler tine held by a student, horses watching from their stalls.
scene [86e7ce] = 一位结实的教授向一个学生手里的深色鹿角尖深深鞠躬，马儿们从隔栏里看着。
# en: Bow back
opt.left.label [9e67be] = 也鞠一躬
# en: You bow to the tine too, which feels silly, and then doesn't. Brask straightens and nods. "You'll do," she says, which from her is a sonnet.
opt.left.say.1 [267bf8] = 你也向鹿角尖鞠了一躬，感觉有点傻，然后就不觉得了。布拉斯克直起身，点点头。“你还行，”她说，从她嘴里出来，这就是一首十四行诗了。
# en: Ask why she bowed
opt.right.label [ffe803] = 问她为什么鞠躬
# en: "It's not yours," she says. "It's lent. The stag lends it to people it means to see again." She looks at you hard. "Don't make it regret that."
opt.right.say.1 [1d1c49] = “它不是你的，”她说。“是借给你的。影鹿把它借给它想再见到的人。”她狠狠地看着你。“别让它后悔。”

@event item_heartwood_tobias
# en: It Hums
title [3bb277] = 它在嗡嗡响
# en: You walk into the greenhouses with the heartwood wand, and every plant in the place leans toward it. Tobias looks up from his potting. "Oh," he says. "Oh, they like that. It's humming. Can you hear it? It's humming to them."
text [5376b2] = 你带着心木魔杖走进温室，里面每一株植物都朝它倾过去。托比亚斯从花盆前抬起头。“噢，”他说。“噢，它们喜欢这个。它在嗡嗡响。你听得见吗？它在对它们哼歌。”
# en: A large gentle student in a greenhouse surrounded by potted plants all leaning toward a red-gold wand in another student's hand.
scene [b594ad] = 温室里，一个高大温和的学生被盆栽围着，所有植物都朝另一个学生手里的红金色魔杖倾斜。
# en: Let him listen
opt.left.label [ab5757] = 让他听
# en: Tobias holds the wand to his ear with his eyes shut and smiles. "It says it's far from home," he says. "But it doesn't mind." The plants agree. You almost hear it.
opt.left.say.1 [9a3831] = 托比亚斯闭着眼把魔杖贴在耳边，笑了。“它说它离家很远，”他说。“不过它不在意。”植物们也同意。你几乎也听见了。
# en: Get on with your work
opt.right.label [ccacf4] = 干你自己的活
# en: You put the wand away and get on with your herbology. The plants lean back to their own business, disappointed, and so does Tobias.
opt.right.say.1 [4b0677] = 你把魔杖收起来，继续做你的草药课作业。植物们失望地回到自己的事情上去，托比亚斯也是。

@event item_thorn_wants
# en: It Wants to Be Used
title [9b19f6] = 它想被用
# en: You wake at night with the thorn wand in your hand and no memory of picking it up. It's warm. It's telling you, in the way wands tell you things, how much stronger you could be by morning. There's a potted fern on the windowsill.
text [0d1056] = 你半夜醒来，手里握着荆棘魔杖，却不记得自己拿起过它。它是温的。它在告诉你——魔杖就是这样告诉你事情的——到早上你能变得多强。窗台上有一盆蕨。
# en: A blackthorn wand lying on a dormitory desk at night, faintly green at its heart, thorns bristling toward a sleeping student.
scene [13f191] = 夜里，一根黑刺李魔杖躺在宿舍桌上，杖心泛着淡淡的绿，尖刺朝着一个熟睡的学生竖起。
# en: Put it away in a drawer
opt.left.label [cb2b9e] = 把它锁进抽屉
# en: You shut it in the drawer and lie awake listening to it not be quiet. In the morning the fern is fine. You're not, quite.
opt.left.say.1 [dc9e73] = 你把它关进抽屉，躺着听它不肯安静。早上，那盆蕨好好的。你却不太好。
# en: Just the fern
opt.right.label [a47f05] = 就那盆蕨
# en: The fern greys. You feel wonderful, and then you look at the fern. The thorn wand is cool again, satisfied, for now.
opt.right.say.1 [746d8d] = 蕨变灰了。你感觉好极了，然后你看了看那盆蕨。荆棘魔杖又凉了下来，满足了，暂时。

@event item_thorn_brask
# en: Brask Smells It
title [9ba827] = 布拉斯克闻出来了
# en: Professor Brask stops beside you and sniffs, like a horse. "Thorn," she says. "Blackthorn. Where did you get it?" She holds out her hand. "I know that wand. I know the woman who cuts them. Give it to me, and I'll snap it, and we'll say no more."
text [adbe8b] = 布拉斯克教授在你身边停下，像马一样嗅了嗅。“荆棘，”她说。“黑刺李。你从哪儿弄来的？”她伸出手。“我认得那种魔杖。我认得削它的那个女人。给我，我把它折了，这事就不提了。”
# en: A stern professor in a stable holding out her hand for a blackthorn wand, a student hesitating.
scene [a12a93] = 马厩里，一位严厉的教授伸手要一根黑刺李魔杖，一个学生犹豫着。
# en: Hand it over
opt.left.label [5e3c6d] = 交给她
# en: Brask snaps it over her knee. It screams, very faintly. "Good," she says, and drops the pieces in the stove, and gives you a hippogriff to muck out, as a kindness.
opt.left.say.1 [c6d46d] = 布拉斯克把它在膝盖上一折。它尖叫了，很轻很轻。“好，”她说，把碎片扔进炉子，然后派给你一只鹰头马身有翼兽去清理马粪，这算是一种好意。
# en: Argue you can handle it
opt.right.label [7ee39b] = 争辩说你能驾驭它
# en: "Can you," says Brask flatly. She doesn't take it. She doesn't say anything else, either, and she doesn't need to.
opt.right.say.1 [653dcc] = “你能吗，”布拉斯克平平地说。她没拿走它。她也没再说别的，她也不需要说。

@event item_thorn_snap
# en: Snap It
title [d6e9fa] = 折断它
# en: Alone on the ramparts, at midnight, you take out the thorn wand and look at it. It knows what you're thinking. It's very still, the way a cat is still.
text [75c0d5] = 午夜，你独自站在城墙上，拿出荆棘魔杖看着它。它知道你在想什么。它非常安静，像猫那样安静。
# en: A student alone on a castle rampart at midnight, holding a blackthorn wand bent nearly to breaking.
scene [faf4c6] = 午夜，一个学生独自站在城堡城墙上，手里的黑刺李魔杖弯得几乎要断了。
# en: Snap it
opt.left.label [87381a] = 折断它
# en: It takes both hands. It doesn't want to go, and then it goes, with a crack like ice. You drop the pieces over the parapet and feel lighter than you have in months.
opt.left.say.1 [9c6449] = 要用两只手。它不想走，然后它走了，咔嚓一声，像冰裂开。你把碎片扔下城墙，几个月来从没觉得这么轻松。
# en: Not yet
opt.right.label [8dd27c] = 还不是时候
# en: You put it away. It's warm against your side all the way back to bed, purring, if wands purr.
opt.right.say.1 [d3cb4f] = 你把它收了起来。回床的一路上它都暖暖地贴着你，在打呼噜——如果魔杖会打呼噜的话。

@event item_locket_midnight
# en: The Locket Opens
title [f63677] = 吊盒打开了
# en: At the twelfth bell the moonpetal locket opens in your hand on its own. The pressed petal inside glows, very faintly, and for a moment you smell the Hush: cold stone, moonlight, silence.
text [029816] = 第十二声钟响时，月瓣吊盒在你手里自己打开了。里面压干的花瓣发着光，非常微弱，有那么一刻你闻到了寂境的气味：冰冷的石头，月光，寂静。
# en: A plain silver locket opening on its own in a student's palm at midnight, a pressed silver flower glowing inside.
scene [e4f70c] = 午夜，一只朴素的银吊盒在学生掌心里自己打开，里面一朵压干的银色花朵发着光。
# en: Close it gently
opt.left.label [21892d] = 轻轻合上
# en: You close it. The glow stays on your fingers for a while, like pollen.
opt.left.say.1 [f8ec41] = 你把它合上了。那光在你指尖上留了一会儿，像花粉。
# en: Let it glow
opt.right.label [a8f060] = 让它亮着
# en: You hold it open until the glow fades, and you're full of quiet, and very cold, and you sleep badly and well.
opt.right.say.1 [ac803e] = 你一直开着它，直到光芒褪去，你满心安静，浑身冰冷，睡得既糟糕又安稳。

@event item_silk_corvin
# en: Corvin Is Jealous
title [7d6f3d] = 科尔文嫉妒了
# en: Corvin walks round you twice. "That," he says, "is Spinner silk. You can't buy Spinner silk. You have to..." He stops. "You didn't." He looks at you with a whole new kind of respect, and also as if calculating what the robe would fetch.
text [00284e] = 科尔文绕着你走了两圈。“那个，”他说，“是织网者的丝。织网者的丝是买不到的。你得……”他停住了。“你不会吧。”他看你的眼神里多了一种全新的敬意，也像在盘算这件长袍能卖多少钱。
# en: A lanky student in a patched coat circling another student in a shimmering grey silk robe, looking deeply envious.
scene [ef88b7] = 一个穿着打补丁外套的瘦高学生绕着另一个穿闪光灰色丝袍的学生打转，满脸羡慕。
# en: Let him touch the sleeve
opt.left.label [c7fa68] = 让他摸摸袖子
# en: He touches the sleeve with one finger, reverently. "I would sell my grandfather's deck for this," he says. "Don't tell him I said that. He's dead. He'd still mind."
opt.left.say.1 [5f91ff] = 他用一根手指碰了碰袖子，满怀敬畏。“为了这个，我愿意卖掉我爷爷的牌，”他说。“别告诉他我说过这话。他已经死了。他还是会介意的。”
# en: Keep it out of his reach
opt.right.label [3dfc7d] = 别让他够着
# en: You step back. Corvin grins. "Smart," he says. "I'd have had it off you by Thursday."
opt.right.say.1 [9bf958] = 你退后一步。科尔文咧嘴一笑。“聪明，”他说。“不然星期四之前我就把它从你身上弄走了。”

@event item_grimoire_isolde
# en: The Headmistress Asks
title [298912] = 院长问起
# en: The headmistress stops you on the stair. She doesn't look at you. She looks at the black grimoire. "Absalom Vrell," she says. "Expelled long before my time. His name is still in the ledger, crossed out. I wondered when he'd find a way to give that away." Now she looks at you. "What do you mean to do with it?"
text [0f7a77] = 院长在楼梯上拦住了你。她没看你。她看着那本黑色魔典。“阿布萨隆·弗雷尔，”她说。“早在我来之前就被开除了。他的名字还在名册上，被划掉了。我一直在想，他什么时候会找到办法把那东西送出去。”现在她看向你。“你打算拿它做什么？”
# en: A silver-haired headmistress on a castle stair, looking at a black-bound book in a student's hands, her face very still.
scene [157bc3] = 城堡楼梯上，一位银发的院长看着学生手里一本黑色封皮的书，脸上一动不动。
# en: Offer it to her
opt.left.label [48f690] = 把它交给她
# en: She takes it without touching the pages and locks it in a drawer. "Thank you," she says. "Some things are safest where people can see them not being used." She means it as praise. You think.
opt.left.say.1 [51a8b5] = 她接过去，没碰书页，把它锁进了抽屉。“谢谢你，”她说。“有些东西，放在人们能看见它没被使用的地方，才最安全。”她这是在夸你。你想。
# en: Keep it, and say so
opt.right.label [03f1dd] = 留着它，并且直说
# en: She looks at you for a long time. "Then use it as he never did," she says, "carefully." She doesn't ask for it again. That's somehow worse.
opt.right.say.1 [8dc34a] = 她看了你很久。“那就用它做他从没做过的事，”她说，“小心地用。”她没再要过它。这反而更糟。
